# Intent: The unit half of the clock styles (docs/design/clock-styles.md, UX14): the clock style 2, date and time, is a valid saved value (self.face.set_config clock_style takes digits, ring or date_time; the saved byte keeps its place, so an older 0 or 1 reads the same), and the clock page's three host calls work on the unit. clock_style() reads the face configuration, clock_set_style() changes it in memory at once and writes the flash once, 700 ms after the last tap, on the application task and only when the style differs from what flash holds, and asleep() is true while the screen is dimmed below the level the person saved (the unit has no other sleep state: a host that puts it to sleep dims the screen, and a person's touch restores it).
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: a tap on the clock page cycles the three styles and wraps; three quick taps cause one write; after a restart the clock page opens in the last style; with the screen dimmed by the host the page shows the sleep sign and a tap only wakes it; self.face.get_config shows clock_style.
# Kconfig: none
# Memory cost: none (one esp timer, created on the first tap).

